tool.help:
**What it does**
Runs ShigaPass on assemblies to tell whether each isolate is *Shigella*, EIEC or neither, and predicts its serotype. One row per assembly, always: if ShigaPass fails on one, the reason is in ``warnings``.
**Also run Mykrobe genotyping (optional)**
Set this to *Yes* and give the reads collection to also get the Mykrobe genotype and QRDR calls and the **combined report** with cross-check warnings, the same as running *Mykrobe Shigella genotyping* and *Combine Shigella report* separately. Assemblies and reads are matched by element name; a sample with only one of them still gets a row. Mykrobe tries the scheme matching the ShigaPass call first and runs the other one too if it does not match.
**Output columns (ShigaPass report)**
sample, rfb, rfb_hits, rfb_pct, mlst_st, fliC, crispr, ipaH, predicted_serotype, predicted_flexserotype, comments (ShigaPass's own fields), species_shigapass, serotype_shigapass (readable), warnings, shigapass_version, tool_version.
The combined report and its warnings are described in *Combine Shigella report*.
